                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e26a471f-15ad-495c-b3e4-1515b481d441",
                                                "sense_id": "85bd9c7c-1fbf-3bdd-94c3-bef72286a013",
                                                "text": "For example, the Sumerologist Jacobsen places the poem in which the young Inanna, still a maiden in puberty, asks a court musician to help her compose a poem to her vulva, in the middle of the cycle, at a point in time when she is recalling the early days when she first chose Dumuzi as her spouse; yet in the poem she is clearly inquiring who will become her lover, and so I place it as part of the beginning: a poem about the virginal Inanna in meditation on the mysteries of her own vulva."
